// pfodWeb NOTE (verified 2026-07-14): all three tags confirmed against the
// official pins_arduino.h in espressif/arduino-esp32:
// https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/blob/master/variants/adafruit_metro_esp32s3/pins_arduino.h
// which defines "#define PIN_BUTTON1 0 // BOOT0 switch", "#define
// LED_BUILTIN 13", and "#define PIN_NEOPIXEL 46" verbatim.
// GPIO0 tagged "button" - confirmed onboard BOOT0/DFU pushbutton
// (Adafruit's own "Read a Push-button" guide, silkscreen labeled "Boot":
// https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-metro-esp32-s3/read-a-push-button).
// GPIO13 tagged "led_high" - confirmed active-high "L" LED (Adafruit's
// own Blink guide: digitalWrite(led, HIGH) turns it on).
// GPIO46 tagged "led_neopixel" - confirmed onboard addressable NeoPixel
// (PIN_NEOPIXEL, silkscreen labeled "Neo"; Adafruit NeoPixel LED guide:
// https://learn.adafruit.com/adafruit-metro-esp32-s3/neopixel-led).
// Cross-check note: an unrelated third-party GitHub fork (avencan/
// Aventen-S3-Sync_ArduinoSupport, a stale mirror of arduino-esp32 used for
// unrelated Aventen board support) carries an outdated copy of this same
// pins_arduino.h with PIN_NEOPIXEL=45 and different SPI pins. The
// actively-maintained espressif/arduino-esp32 master branch (linked above,
// the actual upstream this board.json is sourced from) is authoritative
// and shows PIN_NEOPIXEL=46, matching the existing tag - no correction
// needed.
